{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["Blessings of your father have prevailed over the blessings of my parents — the blessings of your father Jacob, with which the Holy One, blessed be He, blessed me, as it is written: ״והנה יהוה נצב עליו״ and so forth — have prevailed over the blessings of the mountains, as it is written there: ״ופרצת ימה וקדמה״ and so forth — a good inheritance and without constraints, better than all the mountains of the world." "עד תאות — until the end." "גבעות עולם — like the language of ״והתאויתם״, ״תתאו לבא חמת״. And the blessings of Moshe prove this verse, for הורי is a doubling expression for גבעות עולם, as it is written there: ״ומראש הררי קדם וממגד גבעות עולם״, and those blessings shall be לראש יוסף." "נזיר אחיו — king over his brothers."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved הורי as 'my parents' (i.e., Abraham and Isaac who blessed Jacob), understanding Rashbam's reading of the phrase."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:53.717801677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}